// An UNCALLED lambda whose body calls its function-typed parameter. RUNS since D1474 closed:
// `collectCloSigs` walks every lifted function's own arena type, so a lambda's parameter
// interns its `$fnsig` the way a `function` declaration's parameter annotation always did.
//
// Kept as a regression pin rather than a gap. Four ingredients decided the refusal, each
// verified before the close: the LAMBDA spelling (`function apply(f: (i32) => i32): i32`
// always ran), the parameter being CALLED in the body, the parameter's type being a FUNCTION
// type, and the lambda itself being UNCALLED. Any unrelated arity-1 call in the module, or an
// annotation on the binding, also made it run — the mechanism stated as a control. See D1474.
// Should print 7.
const apply = (f: (i32) => i32) => f(1)

print(7)
